wikicache/
candidate_edges.csv
# Character portraits are screencaps belonging to ABC/Shondaland, not facts.
# They stay out of GIT specifically -- history is forever and a takedown would
# mean a rewrite, whereas the deployed copy is one line in .gitlab-ci.yml.
#
# They ARE published on the Pages site, deliberately, with an attribution line
# in the About dialog naming the rights holders and disclaiming ownership. If
# you would rather not serve them at all, delete the portraits copy from the
# pages job; the chart falls back to name-only cards, which is how it worked
# before portraits existed.
portraits/
# Build artifact. CI regenerates it for the live site, and a local build embeds
# portrait paths that only exist on the machine that cached them -- committing
# it would mean broken images for anyone cloning, plus churn on every rebuild.
greys_network.html
node_modules/
__pycache__/

# Build artifacts
table.html
drift_report.md

# Episode-page cache: same reasoning as wikicache -- CC-BY-SA prose we read
# facts out of, never republish.
episodecache/*
# ...except the index, which is Show/Season/Episode/Title -- facts, not the
# CC-BY-SA prose the rest of the directory holds. revwatch.py needs it to know
# WHICH episode pages to ask the API about, and without it in CI the watch list
# silently shrank to character pages and reported all 681 episodes as deleted.
# A negation cannot escape an ignored DIRECTORY, so the glob has to be the
# entry rather than `episodecache/`.
!episodecache/index.csv
